;; The RTS's C API for Haskell called from C (HES60 (a), doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md "As built: HE6's second
;; half"): the foreign stubs GHC writes for a module's foreign exports and "wrapper" imports (bin/hsi stubs-build's
;; stubprobe --stubs, compiled by ci with the program's own C) call rts_lock, rts_mk*, rts_apply, rts_inCall, rts_get*
;; and read ghc_hs_iface's closures and stable_ptr_table; here those are hsi's. A HaskellObj is a word standing for a
;; machine value (hobj: an address of a region no mapping has), a closure label X_closure the stub names (a foreign
;; export's helper, $fstable...) a word for the global it names, and rts_inCall runs the IO action on a thread of its own
;; to its end, the caller's thread suspended in its foreign call (a safe call's semantics, as the non-threaded RTS's).
;; createAdjustor makes a function of ci's text that calls the wrapper's stub with the stable pointer first.


